                                            <div class="col-xl-8 col-lg-10" style="width: 100%;">
                                                <div class="faq__wrap faq__wrap-three">
                                                    <div class="accordion" id="immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-accordion">
                                                        <div class="accordion-item">
                                                            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                                                <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseOne" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseOne">1. What is the main difference between embassy attestation and local MOFA validation?</button>
                                                            </h2>
                                                            <div id="immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-accordion">
                                                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                                                    <p>The variations lie in the explicit sovereign authority verifying the document at individual stages of the validation chain. Virtuo manages this sequence correctly because an embassy or consulate confirms that a document issued in their home country is authentic, whereas the local Ministry of Foreign Affairs provides the final federal stamp required to make that document legally binding and enforceable inside the UAE.</p>
                                                                </div>
                                                            </div>
                                                        </div>
                                                        <div class="accordion-item">
                                                            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                                                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseTwo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseTwo">2. Can Virtuo process consulate services if the document holder is currently outside the UAE?</button>
                                                            </h2>
                                                            <div id="immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-accordion">
                                                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                                                    <p>Yes, absolutely. Virtuo acts as your complete global proxy, meaning you do not need to travel, manage international courier legs, or be physically present to clear your files. You simply hand over your target certificates to our corporate team, and we securely coordinate the entire multi-country embassy and ministry submission loop on your behalf.</p>
                                                                </div>
                                                            </div>
                                                        </div>
                                                        <div class="accordion-item">
                                                            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                                                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseThree" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseThree">3. Why do consulates reject certain corporate or personal documents?</button>
                                                            </h2>
                                                            <div id="immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-accordion">
                                                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                                                    <p>Foreign missions strictly reject documents that feature any form of lamination, physical tears, handwritten corrections, or missing preliminary notary signatures from the country of origin. Virtuo isolates your files from rejection risks by conducting meticulous pre-audits on the physical condition and structural seals of your paperwork before any formal submission is made.</p>
                                                                </div>
                                                            </div>
                                                        </div>
                                                        <div class="accordion-item">
                                                            <h2 class="accordion-header">
                                                                <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseFour" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseFour">4. Do consulate-attested documents require legal translation?</button>
                                                            </h2>
                                                            <div id="immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-collapseFour" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#immigration-residency-solutions-consulate-services-dubai-accordion">
                                                                <div class="accordion-body">
                                                                    <p>Yes, local ministries and judicial departments require all foreign-language records to feature court-approved legal translation to be accepted for official use. Virtuo secures your complete compliance pipeline by directly linking our certified legal translation services into your consular attestation files, delivering completely bilingual, court-ready document packets.</p>
                                                                </div>
                                                            </div>
                                                        </div>
